       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the maximum recommended metformin dose. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A dose this high carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal renal function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO TID with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1000 mg PO BID with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **1700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg BID\n\nIf 1700 mg TID is intentional, tell me and I'll enter it with a note that it's a confirmed above-maximum dose. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
